---
code: whylog-corrupt
when-fires: `dorc why --last` found a durable but it is truncated or otherwise unparseable (a partial write, a clobbered file). plan/whylog.rs parse (`inv-no-throw`: malformed bytes are DATA, never a panic).
why: inv-no-throw: a corrupt durable is diagnostics, never a crash — the reader refuses politely and names the parse-failure reason. Pull-surface: Warning, Floor::None. The reason is typed: four WhylogCorruptReason variants, each with its own prose-component, which the `{reason}` hole renders (28L rul-reason-enums-not-sibling-codes). Remediation register (help) wanted: the durable is damaged — re-run the live analysis to regenerate it.
owns:
  - whylog-corrupt-end-sentinel-missing
---
-- .whylog --
dorc-whylog/2 nonce=dorc attempt=0 host=fixture target=width-one generation=width-one mode=plan started=- @@dorc@@

-- replay --
$ dorc why --last --whylog=.whylog
whylog: warning[whylog-corrupt]: the saved why-log is damaged and cannot be read
back (no dorc-whylog-end sentinel (a truncated write?))
   = help:  this usually means an interrupted write; re-run `dorc why` live, and
            the next plan or apply will save a fresh why-log

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: whylog-corrupt
{{reason}} = "no dorc-whylog-end sentinel (a truncated write?)"
